  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "my oven fan keeps going after ive turned the oven off, been about 20 mins now. is it broken??"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "No, it is not broken. This is completely normal behaviour for most modern ovens. The fan you hear running after switching off is the cooling fan, which keeps working to cool down the electronics and controls until the oven has reached a safe temperature. It typically runs for 10–30 minutes depending on how hot the oven was. It will stop automatically once cooled. You only need to worry if it continues running long after the oven is cold (e.g., an hour later) or makes loud grinding noises."
  }
